From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000057 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Veloce PDFium Patches <veloce-pdfium@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add holder-space spatial index to path display-list replay

Patch 0056 caches ordered RenderPlan skeleton metadata, but each compiled
PathRun still replays by scanning every path node and then rejecting nodes
outside the device tile clip. For sparse high-zoom tiles on huge path pages,
that keeps replay O(total nodes) instead of O(visible candidates).

This patch adds a bounded holder-space grid to the existing path display-list
backend:

* The index is built once at compile time from each node's holder-space bbox.
* Replay transforms the device clip back to holder space, queries candidate
  bins, sorts node ids back into display-list order, then runs the existing
  replay body unchanged.
* Broad preview/whole-page clips, tiny lists, invalid matrices, and invalid
  indexes fall back to the old full scan.
* Very large node bboxes are tracked as overflow candidates so the grid cannot
  drop content.

Correctness invariant: the spatial index only selects candidate nodes inside
one already-compiled ordered PathRun. It never reorders drawing, crosses
RenderPlan barriers, changes eligibility, changes paint/clip/blend handling, or
skips the existing device-clip intersection check.
---
